{
  "id": "minimum-swaps-for-couples",
  "questionId": "minimum-swaps-for-couples",
  "slug": "minimum-swaps-for-couples",
  "title": "Minimum Swaps to Seat Couples Together",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Union find",
  "patterns": [
    "union find",
    "connected components"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "map every person p to their couple id p / 2, since that's the unit that actually matters",
    "look at each occupied seat pair (2k, 2k+1); the two people sitting there belong to some couple ids a and b - union a and b, since these two couples are entangled by the current seating",
    "after processing every seat pair, each connected group of couple ids of size s needs exactly s - 1 swaps to untangle",
    "sum (component size - 1) over every connected component to get the total minimum swaps"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "unioning person ids directly instead of their couple ids (p / 2), which loses the structure that makes the size formula work",
    "forgetting that a seat pair already holding a couple still needs to be processed, since it unions a couple id with itself (a harmless no-op) rather than being skipped incorrectly",
    "trying to simulate actual swaps instead of computing the answer directly from component sizes"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are n couples (2n people total, ids 0 to 2n-1) seated in a row of 2n seats. For any person p, their partner is the other person in couple `p / 2` (using integer division), so people 0 and 1 are a couple, 2 and 3 are a couple, and so on. You're given `row`, an array of length 2n where `row[i]` is the id of the person currently sitting in seat i. In one swap you may pick any two people and swap their seats.\n\n**Return the minimum number of swaps needed so that every couple ends up sitting in adjacent seats (seats 2k and 2k+1 for some k).**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "2n == row.length, 2 <= n <= 30",
      "row is a permutation of 0 to 2n-1"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a single couple, already seated together",
      "a single couple, not seated together",
      "every couple already correctly seated",
      "a long chain of couples that are seated in a rotated order relative to each other, requiring multiple swaps"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "row = [0,2,1,3]",
        "output": "1",
        "expectedOutput": "1",
        "explanation": "swapping seats 1 and 2 puts couple (0,1) and couple (2,3) each next to their partner"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "row = [3,2,0,1]",
        "output": "0",
        "expectedOutput": "0",
        "explanation": "couple (2,3) and couple (0,1) are already seated together"
      },
